{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773077069,"nonce":"ROh42CTXZy4+U86wxRwlBmT/ja8=","title":"ReactFlow dimensions changes trigger spurious auto-save on first render","message":"onNodesChange in graphStore marks isDirty: true for any change where change.type \\!== \"select\". ReactFlow emits \"dimensions\" type changes on first render as it measures node sizes. This triggers an auto-save on page load, writing the loaded state back to the backend unnecessarily.\n\nShould add \"dimensions\" to the excluded change types alongside \"select\":\n  dirty = changes.some(c =\u003e c.type \\!== \"select\" \u0026\u0026 c.type \\!== \"dimensions\")\n\nLow priority since the spurious write is harmless (same data), but wastes a PUT request on every page load.","files":null}]}